# The redirector sends a client to the data server's address of the kind that the client
# came with: [::1] for one that came over IPv6, which neon, in gfal2, does not match with
# the certificate's addresses, and 127.0.0.1 for one that came over IPv4
STORAGE_URL=davs://127.0.0.1:1094/srv/x/interop
READY_TIMEOUT=120
# The cluster's own copies, where gfal2 sends the COPY to it: XRootD redirects a COPY to
# [::1] whatever the client came with (XrdHttpTpc's RedirectTransfer), so gfal2 cannot
# follow it. Its data server copies the same way as the standalone XRootD of run.sh.
SKIP=^xrootd-cluster( pulls from weed| pushes to weed|'s pulled copy matches)$|^weed's pushed copy matches$
